(EXP-100: undocumented precision on LANGUAGE.md:2062 - a base outside 2 to 36
 is rejected at COMPILE time, not at run time, and not silently clamped.
 The manual says which bases are supported but never says what happens to an
 unsupported one, so this row records the answer rather than a claim. It also
 means a leaf that draws a random base must draw it from 2 to 36 or the
 generated program will not compile at all.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox EXP-100.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   error: Only base 2 through base 36 are supported
   no binary produced; compile error
)
a text called digits is "11".
Print digits as a base 37 number.
